["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>In open Interior country you find more deer with your eyes than with your boots. <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Glassing\">Glassing</button> lets you see them before they see you.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-distance.jpg\" alt=\"Find the deer: grey bodies, white rumps, big ears.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Find the deer: grey bodies, white rumps, big ears. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: BLM Oregon &amp; Washington, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_deer_in_eastern_Oregon_(29844645086).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Sit, brace, glass slowly in strips. Look for parts of deer.</li></ul>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"3\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Get steady glass</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 3</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Binocular setup at home. Twist the eye cups to fit your eyes. Set the right eye dial, the diopter, so both eyes are sharp. Mark the setting with a dab of paint or tape.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"110\" y=\"80\" width=\"70\" height=\"150\" rx=\"20\"/><rect x=\"220\" y=\"80\" width=\"70\" height=\"150\" rx=\"20\"/>\n    <rect x=\"178\" y=\"110\" width=\"44\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"116\" y=\"62\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"226\" y=\"62\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"130\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"226\" y=\"96\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"258\" cy=\"102\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#ffd34d\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Set up once, at home</text>\n  <path d=\"M110 70 L60 60\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Eye cups</text>\n  <path d=\"M290 102 L320 102\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"324\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Right eye</text><text x=\"324\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">dial</text>\n  <path d=\"M186 130 L60 170\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Focus wheel</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark the dial setting with a paint dot</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Set eye cups and the right eye dial once, at home.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of a seated hunter glassing: back against a pack or tree, knees up, elbows resting on the knees, binoculars at the eyes. Braced and still.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"70\" y=\"140\" width=\"50\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"95\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pack</text>\n  <path d=\"M130 250 L140 160\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"22\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"128\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M140 230 L210 190 L250 250\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"18\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n  <path d=\"M146 168 L206 186 L172 132\" stroke=\"#4a5a3c\" stroke-width=\"10\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n  <rect x=\"164\" y=\"118\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"186\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Elbows on knees</text>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Back on pack</text>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Sit still</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brace: shaking glass hides deer</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Sit. Elbows on knees, back on a pack or tree.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Low sun in front of you causes glare in the lenses. A hat brim or your hand held above the binoculars shades the glass.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"80\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" opacity=\".6\"><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"140\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"160\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"160\" r=\"40\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 116 L200 116 L200 126 L80 130 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n  <rect x=\"146\" y=\"146\" width=\"56\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M200 116 L230 150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">hat brim shades</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Low sun ahead? Shade the glass</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brim or a hand above the lenses</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Better: glass with the sun behind you</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Low sun ahead? Shade the lenses.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Move the binoculars, not your eyes inside them (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: binocular technique in full</summary><ul><li>Set the eye cups and the right eye dial (diopter) once at home. Mark the setting.</li><li>Brace. Elbows on knees, back on a tree or pack. Shaking binoculars hide deer.</li><li>Hold still and let the view settle. Move the binoculars, not your eyes inside them (Tip).</li><li>Look through the binoculars for a long time, rest your eyes for a few seconds, then go back (Tip).</li><li>Use a hat brim or hand to cut glare when the sun is low in front of you.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two binocular views of the same deer at 800 metres. Left, handheld: the view shakes, the deer is a blur, the tail flick is missed. Right, on a tripod: the view is still and the small tail flick is easy to see.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"140\" r=\"54\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"140\" r=\"54\"/><circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"140\" r=\"54\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"140\" r=\"54\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"><ellipse cx=\"96\" cy=\"146\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\"/><ellipse cx=\"104\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"152\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\" opacity=\".5\"><path d=\"M40 90 l10 6 l-8 6 l10 6\"/><path d=\"M160 90 l-10 6 l8 6 l-10 6\"/></g>\n  <ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"146\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"316\" cy=\"136\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M282 142 l-10 -10\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><path d=\"M282 142 l-10 -10\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"276\" cy=\"136\" r=\"10\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Handheld</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tripod</text>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">shaky blur</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tail flick seen</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same deer, 800 m (875 yd) away (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A tripod steadies the view and stops arm fatigue <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Use the binoculars you have plus a cheap tripod adapter. Upgrade glass later.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tripods in full</summary><ul><li>A tripod steadies the binoculars and stops arm fatigue on long sessions <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Many western hunters rate a tripod as a bigger upgrade than better glass (60%, hunter opinion).</li><li>A light tripod and a binocular adapter is enough to start.</li><li>Steady glass shows small movement: a tail flick at 800 m (875 yd) you would miss handheld (Tip).</li><li>My lean in full: start with the binoculars you have plus a cheap tripod adapter. Upgrade glass later, once you know what you use.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DF0glPzsT74\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>The KEY to Glassing for Elk and Deer With a Spotting Scope</b><small>Binoculars find the animal, the spotting scope judges it.<br>Cliff Gray, YouTube, 6 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of the grid method. A binocular view moves across a hillside in slow strips, stopping at each spot. Near strip left to right, middle strip right to left, far strip left to right. Each view overlaps the last by about a third, leaving no gaps. On the far strip it stops on two ears showing above a bush: a bedded deer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <path d=\"M0 270 L0 80 Q 90 30 170 60 Q 250 20 320 50 Q 370 64 400 56 L400 270 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"40,120 50,92 60,120\"/><polygon points=\"58,128 68,100 78,128\"/><polygon points=\"180,96 190,68 200,96\"/><polygon points=\"330,200 340,172 350,200\"/><polygon points=\"110,210 120,182 130,210\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"342\" cy=\"112\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"10\"/><ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"9\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"234\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"9\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M336 104 l-6 -10 l8 4 Z M346 104 l6 -10 l-8 4 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"270\" width=\"400\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Slow strips, overlap a third, no gaps</text>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.24s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.04s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.84s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.64s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.44s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"228\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.24s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.04s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.84s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.64s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7.44s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"166\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8.24s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"9.04s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"9.84s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"10.64s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"11.44s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"104\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".07\"/></g>\n  <g>\n    <circle cx=\"-20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"60 228;60 228;130 228;130 228;200 228;200 228;270 228;270 228;340 228;340 228;340 166;340 166;270 166;270 166;200 166;200 166;130 166;130 166;60 166;60 166;60 104;60 104;130 104;130 104;200 104;200 104;270 104;270 104;340 104;340 104\" keyTimes=\"0.000;0.067;0.087;0.133;0.153;0.200;0.220;0.267;0.287;0.333;0.353;0.400;0.420;0.467;0.487;0.533;0.553;0.600;0.620;0.667;0.687;0.733;0.753;0.800;0.820;0.867;0.887;0.933;0.953;1.000\" dur=\"12.0s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"11.44s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"80\" y=\"8\" width=\"240\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"29\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two ears in the brush</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Slow strips, a third overlap, stop and look at each view. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Quick scan of open slopes first, then the grid <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Then glass it all again. Deer stand up and move (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the seven grid steps</summary><ol><li>Pick a spot with a wide view and the wind right (see Wind and thermals).</li><li>Quick scan first: open slopes, cut blocks, edges where deer are easy to see <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Then split the view into a grid in your head <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Start at one corner. Glass one strip slowly, left to right <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Overlap each binocular view by about a third so nothing falls in a gap <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Drop down one strip and come back right to left <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Then glass it again. Deer stand up, move and turn as light changes.</li></ol></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ICFJhiR_cxU\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to glass || How to Hunt</b><small>Sit, steady your binoculars and search the slope in a grid.<br>Remi Warren, YouTube, 3 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A hillside split into a 3 by 3 grid. Scan order runs 1 to 9 in a snake pattern: bottom row left to right, middle row right to left, top row left to right. Start near, finish far.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"420\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <path d=\"M10 330 L10 120 Q 90 40 170 80 Q 240 30 310 70 Q 360 90 390 80 L390 330 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <polygon points=\"60,150 70,120 80,150\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"78,160 88,128 98,160\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"250,110 260,82 270,110\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"268,118 278,90 288,118\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"330,250 340,222 350,250\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\" fill=\"none\">\n    <line x1=\"137\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"137\" y2=\"330\"/>\n    <line x1=\"263\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"263\" y2=\"330\"/>\n    <line x1=\"10\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"160\"/>\n    <line x1=\"10\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"245\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <circle cx=\"73\" cy=\"290\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"73\" y=\"298\">1</text>\n    <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"290\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"298\">2</text>\n    <circle cx=\"326\" cy=\"290\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"298\">3</text>\n    <circle cx=\"326\" cy=\"203\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"211\">4</text>\n    <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"203\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"211\">5</text>\n    <circle cx=\"73\" cy=\"203\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"73\" y=\"211\">6</text>\n    <circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"125\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"133\">7</text>\n    <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"125\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"133\">8</text>\n    <circle cx=\"326\" cy=\"125\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"326\" y=\"133\">9</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M92 290 L180 290 M219 290 L306 290\"/>\n    <path d=\"M343 290 Q 370 250 343 210\"/>\n    <path d=\"M306 203 L219 203 M180 203 L92 203\"/>\n    <path d=\"M56 203 Q 30 160 92 130\"/>\n    <path d=\"M128 125 L180 125 M219 125 L306 125\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Far: ridges, benches, timber edges</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"330\" width=\"380\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"358\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"186\" y=\"370\" width=\"28\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"406\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You, sitting, binoculars on a rest</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"352\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Start near</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"352\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">1 to 2 min</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"368\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">per square</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Start near, finish far. 1 to 2 minutes a square.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 320\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What to look for: deer parts, not whole deer. In a timber edge scene: 1 a horizontal back line among vertical trunks, 2 four thin vertical legs under a bush, 3 an ear flicking above grass, 4 a white rump patch, 5 an antler tip catching light.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"30\" width=\"400\" height=\"250\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#6b4f35\"><rect x=\"30\" y=\"40\" width=\"10\" height=\"150\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"40\" width=\"10\" height=\"150\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"40\" width=\"10\" height=\"150\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"40\" width=\"10\" height=\"150\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".75\"><polygon points=\"20,80 35,30 50,80\"/><polygon points=\"60,90 75,34 90,90\"/><polygon points=\"100,84 115,32 130,84\"/><polygon points=\"140,88 155,36 170,88\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"150\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"46\" ry=\"26\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"280\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"200\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"190\" y=\"230\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M300 230 l-6 -14 l10 6 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"238\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M340 110 l6 -18 m-6 18 l-12 -12\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"346\" cy=\"92\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#ffd34d\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <circle cx=\"85\" cy=\"134\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"140\">1</text>\n    <circle cx=\"222\" cy=\"190\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"196\">2</text>\n    <circle cx=\"322\" cy=\"212\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"322\" y=\"218\">3</text>\n    <circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"238\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"244\">4</text>\n    <circle cx=\"370\" cy=\"96\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"102\">5</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Look for parts, not a whole deer</text>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"300\">1 flat back  2 legs  3 ear flick</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"316\">4 white rump  5 antler glint</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Look for <strong>parts</strong>: a flat back, legs, an ear flick, a white rump <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what to look for, in full</summary><ul><li>Do not look for a whole deer. Look for <strong>parts</strong> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>A <strong>horizontal line</strong> in a world of vertical trees: a back or belly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>Vertical legs</strong> under a shape that does not belong <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>An <strong>ear flick</strong> or tail twitch. Movement is the giveaway.</li><li>The <strong>white rump</strong> of a mule deer, or the flash of a white tail (Tip).</li><li>A shape that is the wrong colour: grey brown body against green or yellow.</li><li>Antler tips catching light, or a shiny black nose.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-does-bedded.jpg\" alt=\"Two bedded does: only heads and ears show.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Two bedded does: only heads and ears show. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Bedded_Down_in_Sagebrush_and_Snow_(15523121163).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-buck-bedded.jpg\" alt=\"Bedded buck: the rack shows, the body hides.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bedded buck: the rack shows, the body hides. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Buck_in_Southwest_Wyoming_(23007137314).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bt-bedded.jpg\" alt=\"Bedded buck: head, ears and a back line.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bedded buck: head, ears and a back line. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Buiobuione, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black-tailed_deer_-_Odocoileus_hemionus_columbianus_-_05.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-buck-rear.jpg\" alt=\"From behind: the white rump gives it away.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>From behind: the white rump gives it away. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Buck_(15382465555).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Find each deer, then name the part you saw first.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Glassing plan for a day. Deer activity, a curve, peaks at dawn and dusk and dips at midday. Legal hunting hours for deer run from 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset. Glass open slopes at first light and the last hour, and glass shade, timber edges and benches at midday.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"40\" width=\"320\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"40\" width=\"40\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".15\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"40\" width=\"40\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".15\"/>\n  <path d=\"M40 120 C 60 60, 80 50, 100 60 C 140 90, 160 190, 200 190 C 240 190, 260 90, 300 60 C 320 50, 340 60, 360 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"210\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"228\">sunrise</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"228\">sunset</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"228\">midday</text></g>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 h</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 h</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Legal hours: 1 h before sunrise to 1 h after sunset</text>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">peak</text><text x=\"268\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">peak</text>\n  <rect x=\"12\" y=\"242\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dawn, last hour:</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">open slopes, edges</text>\n  <rect x=\"208\" y=\"242\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday: shade,</text><text x=\"298\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">timber, benches</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Glass at first light and in the last hour (Tip).</li><li>Deer legal hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: times and places in full</summary><ul><li>Deer are most active at dawn and dusk <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Glass first light and the last hour before legal shooting light ends (Tip).</li><li>Legal hunting hours for deer: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (synopsis page 11, item 38) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>You work out sunrise and sunset yourself, for each date and place (synopsis page 12) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Midday: glass shade, timber edges and benches where deer bed (Tip).</li><li>Glass from above, with the sun behind you, so deer are lit and you are not (Tip).</li><li>Near Sun Peaks: cut blocks, burns, open grass slopes and timber edges (Tip, check on your map).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view: the hunter glasses from a high point with the low sun behind them. The far slope and the deer are lit up. The hunter sits in shadow, and the deer would look into the sun to see them.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"60\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" opacity=\".5\"><line x1=\"56\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"150\"/><line x1=\"56\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"190\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M0 300 L0 150 L80 130 L150 260 L230 270 L400 120 L400 300 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M230 270 L400 120 L400 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"122\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"130\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(320 186)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M84 120 L300 180\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 5\"/>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">deer lit up</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sun behind you, glass from above</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">you sit in shade (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Glass from above with the sun behind you. Deer are lit, you are not (Tip).</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Mistake versus right way. Top: one fast sweep across the hillside, like a camera pan, misses a bedded deer. Bottom: slow overlapping views, one after another, land right on the same deer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"100\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#efe2d6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"170\" width=\"380\" height=\"100\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M30 90 L370 90\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><polygon points=\"366,82 366,98 382,90\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(250 112)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-4 -6 l-4 -8 l6 4 Z M4 -6 l4 -8 l-6 4 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Fast pan: deer missed</text>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"3\">\n    <circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"195\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"285\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"230\" r=\"28\" opacity=\".4\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(250 242)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-4 -6 l-4 -8 l6 4 Z M4 -6 l4 -8 l-6 4 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">Slow, overlapping: found</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Overlap each view by about a third (60%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Sit longer than you think. When you want to move, glass it one more time.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Sweeping fast across a hillside, like a camera pan.</li><li>Looking only for a whole standing deer in the open.</li><li>Glassing straight into a rising or setting sun.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Set a 20 minute timer. Glass one hillside with the grid twice. Write down every maybe, then check it.</p></aside>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.gohunt.com/browse/tips-and-tricks/glassing/the-three-pillars-of-glassing-and-how-they-will-help-you-find-more-big-game\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">goHUNT: The three pillars of glassing</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.themeateater.com/hunt/general/what-you-need-to-know-about-glassing-terrain\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MeatEater: What you need to know about glassing terrain</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorbenchmark.com/big-game-hunting/glassing-strategy-guide\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Benchmark: Glassing for big game</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.wideopenspaces.com/heres-glass-mule-deer-increase-odds-filling-tag/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wide Open Spaces: How to glass for mule deer</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.sitkagear.com/experience/what-colors-can-deer-see\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sitka: What colours can deer see (crepuscular activity)</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li></ul><ul><li>Hunt Mentor deer research notes, research/2026-10-01-deer.md (60%, hunter consensus)</li></ul>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly: page 11, item 38 (hunting hours, sunrise and sunset). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Note: glassing is a skill, not a rule. Most points are hunter experience, labelled Tip.</li></ul>"]